ike i i was  crushed  without saying his disapproval i knew  and stunk  and i was right when i walked in here i  knew i wasn't good enough  to go to the school and i thought to  myself ah [ __ ] this school that's stupid  anyway  the first year theater there's a  question  that they ask students from time to time  and it's a make-or-break question and  when we ask this question you don't know  and the question is this  they say why do you want to act  now  if you say anything like i want to be a  star you're not  you're not going to get in i didn't know  that  and i figured i already blew the  audition so i told him the truth he said  why do you want to act i don't  that's what i said  and they said well then why are you here  i said because i want to be a comedian  and some comedian told me that if i want  to be a good comedian i need to learn  how to act  teachers look at each other they go  thank you very much and i left  and i was walking down the hallway  kicking rocks  there was a kid that already went here  his name was ankle handy  and they go said hey man i listen to  them talking about you i said you did he  said you're in i said what he said  you're in  that didn't make any sense  somehow we worked it out so that it gave  me an early enrollment and i left  eastman within weeks of that  and i came to duke ellington and it was  better than i could have ever imagined  i didn't have the suspicion that most  new kids get i was an oddity a new toy  it was quirky it wasn't a snappy dress i  didn't really know what the [ __ ] was  going on because the crack epidemic  itself was new to me and they were all  refugees from the neighborhood schools  [Applause]

